# claude-seat-1: task 1790632442 ("A payout intent past its retry window no longer locks the owner out of every withdrawal, and a bounded reconciliation door exists")

Closes: 1790632442 (done)

## What landed (branch claude/seat-1, on top of main 83f2711; `git merge main` was a no-op, main did not move)

This task was resumed from an executor's uncommitted partial (~1400 lines, 2026-09-29 ~18:35Z). It was reviewed against the brief and CLAUDE.md, one hole was closed, and the rest was completed as below.

- 591517c fix: a payout intent past its retry window no longer locks its owner out of withdraw, and two bounded doors close a stale intent (E-109, review gap 6)
  - (a) `withdraw`: a Payout intent past `retry_deadline_ns` cannot be re-driven, so it no longer counts as a withdrawal in progress. A live payout still refuses. The pending flag is cleared and the stale entry stays on record, with its escrow debit standing.
  - (b) `reconcile_ledger_intent(id, block)`: owner or controller. The caller is captured first, anonymous callers are refused, and the rate limit is shared with `notify_deposit` (`deposit_verification_rate_limited`). It reads the named block through ICP `query_blocks` or ckBTC `get_transactions`, following the archive callback via `define_function!` with a no-archive fallback decode. It settles Moved only when `transfer_proves_intent` holds (memo, created_at_time, from/to per kind, amount; payout = amount - fee). It settles through `settle_intent`, so removal is one-shot and a credit is still behind `claim_deposit_block`.
  - (b) `admin_close_stale_ledger_intent(id, NotMoved | Moved)`: controller only, past the window only. NEW IN THIS SESSION: it also refuses while a lease is live, because a message may still be awaiting the ledger, and a NotMoved refund followed by a real movement would pay twice. Owner and amount come from the entry. NotMoved on a payout refunds the up-front debit; on other kinds it credits nothing. Moved on a payout or refund goes through `book_outgoing_moved`, which is shared with `settle_intent`. Moved on a pull or sweep is refused. No balance setter.
  - `clear_pending_withdrawal_unless_another_payout_is_open` keeps the per-owner flag while another payout is open.
  - `.did` plus the three `src/declarations/table_*/table_*.did` copies gain `StaleIntentClose`, `Result_IntentLine` (declarations copies) and the two methods. The JS/TS bindings were regenerated with `./scripts/check-declarations-js.sh --write`. The declaration drift baseline is unchanged (88 items; the new methods are declared, not baselined).
  - (c) `tests/money_safety/tests/ledger_boundary.rs`: six `e109_*` tests.
    - An Unknown outcome is produced by stopping the ledger. A discarded continuation is produced by `trap_*_tail`.
    - The block door is tested both ways: wrong block, future block, stranger, right block, and once-only.
    - A stale pull is credited once, and `notify_deposit` of the same block is refused.
    - Controller NotMoved refunds a payout; it is refused inside the window and refused for the owner.
    - Controller Moved is refused on a pull; NotMoved on that pull credits nothing.
    - Moved on a payout gives no refund.
    - `withdraw` succeeds beside a stale payout.
  - `tests/money_safety/tests/admin_custody.rs`: the census `AUDITED` gains `admin_close_stale_ledger_intent` with its verdict. The FINDING 07 sweep drives it with both outcomes, and the census would otherwise have gone red.
- f52484d docs: DEFECTS.md E-109 (medium, FIXED) register row above E-108, with the entry at the end of the file. SECURITY-FINDINGS.md FINDING 29 ("needs an operator to reconcile") gains an update note, and FINDING 38 ("kept forever, pending operator reconciliation") gains a parenthesis. Both name the two doors. E-109 was free on main and on every seat branch.
- fec1517 fix(hygiene): `make hygiene` crashed on a CLEAN tree on macOS `/bin/bash` 3.2 (`candidates[@]: unbound variable`: an empty array under `set -u`). This was pre-existing on main, and it hit here because everything was committed. It now uses `${a[@]+"${a[@]}"}`.
- 8b46a5f test(seam): `invariants::seam::seam_honest_play_produces_no_self_reported_failure` went RED in the first `make test`.
  - The error was "start_new_hand failed: Need at least 2 active players with chips".
  - Root cause: the table wasm grew from 2.86 MB to 3.22 MB, past 3 MiB. pocket-ic 11 installs anything over 2 MB in 1 MiB chunks, so there is one more chunk upload, one more round, and every timestamp shifts by +1 ns. That gives a different shuffle, and seat 2 won hands 1 and 2, busting the other two 2-ICP stacks at ICP/2 per street.
  - Main's lib.rs passes the same test, and mine failed 3/3, with no engine change on the path.
  - The post-flop bet is now ICP/10, so all three deals happen on any shuffle.

